{"summary":"Restore lowercase dispatch for in-place string conversion","explanation":"The std::string overload of AsciiStrToLower calls the case-folding helper with ToUpper=true, which explains both reported failures. Change it to false, matching the destination/source overload and preserving the lowercase contract.","edits":[{"path":"absl/strings/ascii.cc","old":"void AsciiStrToLower(std::string* absl_nonnull s) {
  char* p = &(*s)[0];
  return ascii_internal::AsciiStrCaseFold<true>(p, p, s->size());
}","new":"void AsciiStrToLower(std::string* absl_nonnull s) {
  char* p = &(*s)[0];
  return ascii_internal::AsciiStrCaseFold<false>(p, p, s->size());
}"}]}
